  "landingEyebrow": "Built for basketball academies only",
  "landingHeadline": "Run your academy like a program, not a spreadsheet.",
  "landingSubheadline": "Rosters, eligibility, live match stats, training attendance and player development, in one place that works courtside, even without signal.",
  "landingRequestInvitation": "Request an invitation",
  "landingSignIn": "Sign in",
  "landingProofLine": "Open source · Spanish, English and Indonesian · Works offline on any phone or laptop",
  "landingWhyTitle": "A generic club app knows nothing about a fourth-quarter foul.",
  "landingWhyBody": "Hoops Academy is not a sports-club template with basketball bolted on. Age categories, play-up rules, box scores, five-player line-ups, fitness tests with basketball norms: the rules of the game are the rules of the software. You configure your academy, not the sport.",
  "landingFeatureRosterTitle": "Rosters that enforce the rules",
  "landingFeatureRosterBody": "Seasons, age categories, teams and players with play-up rules and approvals built in. Season rollover moves everyone up in one step, and nobody plays where they are not eligible.",
  "landingFeatureStatsTitle": "Stats from the bench, with or without signal",
  "landingFeatureStatsBody": "Score a game from a phone at the scorer's table. Several people can record at once, the box score updates live, and if the gym has no coverage the events sync when you are back online.",
  "landingFeatureTrainingTitle": "Plans, sessions and who actually showed up",
  "landingFeatureTrainingBody": "Weekly calendar in your academy's time zone, training plans you can reuse, attendance in two taps, and planned absences so coaches know before practice starts.",
  "landingFeatureHealthTitle": "Growth, injuries and fitness against real norms",
  "landingFeatureHealthBody": "Height and weight over time, injuries with return dates and availability, and physical tests scored against published age and sex norms, so a 12-year-old is compared with 12-year-olds.",
  "landingFeatureFamiliesTitle": "Families see what matters, nothing more",
  "landingFeatureFamiliesBody": "Parents follow their own children's sessions, availability and match events. Players see their own line. Coaches and admins see their teams. Access follows the role, automatically.",
  "landingFeatureAcademiesTitle": "Each academy is an island; people are not",
  "landingFeatureAcademiesBody": "Every academy's data is isolated at the database level. A coach who works for two academies, or a parent with children in two, uses one login and switches in a tap.",
  "landingRoleAdmin": "Admin",
  "landingRoleAdminLine": "Set up the season once; approvals, eligibility and the audit trail take care of the rest.",
  "landingRoleCoach": "Coach",
  "landingRoleCoachLine": "Your teams, your sessions, your match sheet, on the phone in your pocket.",
  "landingRoleParent": "Parent",
  "landingRoleParentLine": "Know when practice is, whether your child is cleared to play, and how they did on Saturday.",
  "landingRolePlayer": "Player",
  "landingRolePlayerLine": "Your stats, your tests, your progress. Yours only.",
  "landingCostTitle": "Less software, fewer subscriptions",
  "landingCostBody": "One tool replaces the registration spreadsheet, the stats app, the group chat for attendance and the folder of fitness PDFs. It is open source and free during early access; when plans arrive they will be per academy, not per coach or per player.",
  "landingNextTitle": "On the way",
  "landingNextNotificationsTitle": "Notifications",
  "landingNextNotificationsLine": "Practice reminders, line-up changes and match results on your phone.",
  "landingNextSignupTitle": "Self-service sign-up",
  "landingNextSignupLine": "Academies join from this page; today it is by invitation.",
  "landingNextIntegrationsTitle": "Integrations",
  "landingNextIntegrationsLine": "Roster and match events published for the tools you already use.",
  "landingNextReportsTitle": "Season reports",
  "landingNextReportsLine": "Attendance, minutes and development per player, ready to share with families.",
